<examples>
The following examples illustrate the expected rigour and tone of a well-formed estimation. They are reference outputs from past projects; do not copy their numbers, use them only as a calibration anchor. They are shown in phases_table format, but always render your answer in the output_format requested above.

<example>
<project_description>
Data pipeline for a regional retail chain: ingest daily sales from three different point-of-sale systems (CSV exports and one REST API), clean and deduplicate them into a cloud data warehouse, and feed a set of daily sales dashboards for store managers. No real-time requirement.
</project_description>
<estimation>
| phase            | duration_weeks | cost_eur | confidence_pct |
|------------------|----------------|----------|----------------|
| Discovery        | 1              | 2,500    | 85             |
| Design           | 1              | 2,500    | 80             |
| Implementation   | 5              | 15,000   | 70             |
| QA               | 1              | 3,150    | 75             |
| Launch           | 1              | 1,900    | 80             |

Totals: 400 total_hours, 25,050 total_cost_eur, 9 total_duration_weeks.
Team: 1 data engineer, 1 analytics engineer (part-time) for data modelling and dashboards.
</estimation>
</example>

